{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-156596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $L$ be the line with equation $y=-x$ in ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- $L$ contains the zero-vector\n- $L$ is closed under vector addition\n- $L$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $L$ is a subspace of ${R}^{2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-156596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $L$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ -x\\end{aligned}],\\,x\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The coordinates of the zero-vector satisfy the equation $y=-x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-x \\\\ (0) & =-(0) \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Let, for example, $a=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ -a\\end{aligned}]\\in L$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ -b\\end{aligned}]\\in L.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ -a\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ -b\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a+b \\\\ (-a)+(-b)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a+b \\\\ -(a+b)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $y=-x.$ Therefore, $a+b\\in L.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Let, for example, $a=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ -a\\end{aligned}]\\in L$ and $k\\in R.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k\\cdot a & =k\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ -a\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}ka \\\\ k(-a)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}ka \\\\ -(ka)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $y=-x.$ Therefore, $k\\cdot a\\in L.$\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since statements II and III are true, $L$ must be a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"All the statements are true.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-156596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0f9522b895dc6d7dcff4eb5a83a2549db062dfbe62841d36b23ba6e4cdb97767"} {"question" "q-156596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-156596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "All the statements are true"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-156596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "All the statements are true"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-156624" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $L$ be the line with equation $x=2y-1$ in ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $L$ contains the zero-vector\n- $L$ is closed under vector addition\n- $L$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-156624" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $L$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2y-1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is false. The coordinates of the zero-vector do not satisfy the equation $x=2y-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2y-1 \\\\ (0) & =2(0)-1 \\\\ 0 & =-1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Let, for example, $a=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ from $L.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1+1 \\\\ 0+1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nHowever, $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\notin L$ since substituting the coordinates into the equation, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2y-1 \\\\ (0) & =2(1)-1 \\\\ 0 & =1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $0\\notin L,$ this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since statements II and III are false, $L$ is *not* a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-156624" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0f9522b895dc6d7dcff4eb5a83a2549db062dfbe62841d36b23ba6e4cdb97767"} {"question" "q-156624" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-156624" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "IV only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-156624" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "IV only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-157290" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $L$ be the line with equation $2y=3x$ in ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- $L$ contains the zero-vector\n- $L$ is closed under vector addition\n- $L$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-157290" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $L$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}x\\end{aligned}],\\,x\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The coordinates of the zero-vector satisfy the equation $2y=3x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y & =3x \\\\ 2(0) & =3(0) \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Let, for example, $a=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}a\\end{aligned}]\\in L$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}b\\end{aligned}]\\in L.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}a\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}b\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a+b \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}a+\\frac{3}{2}b\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a+b \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}(a+b)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $2y=3x.$ Therefore, $a+b\\in L.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Let, for example, $a=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}a\\end{aligned}]\\in L$ and $k\\in R.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k\\cdot a & =k\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}a\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}ka \\\\ k(\\frac{3}{2}a)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}ka \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}(ka)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $2y=3x.$ Therefore, $k\\cdot a\\in L.$\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since statements II and III are true, $L$ must be a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-157290" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0f9522b895dc6d7dcff4eb5a83a2549db062dfbe62841d36b23ba6e4cdb97767"} {"question" "q-157290" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-157290" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "All the statements are true"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I and IV only"] ["text" "I, II, and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-157290" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-156628" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $L$ be the line with equation $x=5y$ in ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $L$ contains the zero-vector\n- $L$ is closed under vector addition\n- $L$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $L$ is a subspace of ${R}^{2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-156628" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $L$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The coordinates of the zero-vector satisfy the equation $x=5y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5y \\\\ (0) & =5(0) \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Let, for example, $a=[\\begin{aligned}5a \\\\ a\\end{aligned}]\\in L$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}5b \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]\\in L.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =[\\begin{aligned}5a \\\\ a\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5b \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5a+5b \\\\ a+b\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5(a+b) \\\\ a+b\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $x=5y.$ Therefore, $a+b\\in L.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Let, for example, $a=[\\begin{aligned}5a \\\\ a\\end{aligned}]\\in L$ and $k\\in R.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k\\cdot a & =k\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5a \\\\ a\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5ka \\\\ ka\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $x=5y.$ Therefore, $k\\cdot a\\in L.$\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since statements II and III are true, $L$ must be a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"All the statements are true.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-156628" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0f9522b895dc6d7dcff4eb5a83a2549db062dfbe62841d36b23ba6e4cdb97767"} {"question" "q-156628" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-156628" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "All the statements are true"] ["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"]