ion $y=-3x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x \\\\ (0) & =-3(0) \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Let, for example, $a=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ -3a\\end{aligned}]\\in L$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ -3b\\end{aligned}]\\in L.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ -3a\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ -3b\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a+b \\\\ (-3a)+(-3b)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a+b \\\\ -3(a+b)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $y=-3x.$ Therefore, $a+b\\in L.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Let, for example, $a=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ -3a\\end{aligned}]\\in L$ and $k\\in R.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k\\cdot a & =k\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ -3a\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}ka \\\\ k(-3a)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}ka \\\\ -3(ka)\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $y=-3x.$ Therefore, $k\\cdot a\\in L.$\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since statements II and III are true, $L$ must be a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"All the statements are true.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f74c9758bdcc6bdfbcd0"} {"question" "q-156653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0f9522b895dc6d7dcff4eb5a83a2549db062dfbe62841d36b23ba6e4cdb97767"} {"question" "q-156653" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044012/state.json" "file_sha256" "6f6c9a4e3e328d62fe160ed205cab7acff4ab2e33c79f